description:
## Goal

Make fact settledness transitively sound without recalculating a formula whose input content did not change.

Today FactSlot is settled when its own publishers are clean. If A becomes unready while retaining the same current content, a formula B that reads Current(A) can remain locally settled even though A may still move. Scheduler::complete propagates readiness-only movement to Settled and SettledPresence readers, but not through Current readers. Finality is therefore local, not dependency-transitive.

## Output contract

For a formula B that reads Current(A):

- while A is dirty, Settled(B) is unavailable;
- if A concludes with unchanged content, B becomes final again without evaluating B;
- if A's content changes, B evaluates because its recorded input revision moved;
- this readiness dependency propagates through chains and cycles;
- adding or replacing a read updates finality incrementally;
- no cell value is cleared merely to represent unready state.

Finality is dependency state, not a pass. No SCC/group inventory, epoch object, root scan, graph sweep, or reader recomputation may be introduced unless a failing test proves the simpler incremental model insufficient.

## TDD strategy

Start with scheduler-level red tests:

1. A -> B -> C: dirty A without changing content. Settled(C) becomes unavailable; B and C evaluation counts remain unchanged; all become settled again when A concludes unchanged.
2. Same chain with A content movement: only the transitive content readers evaluate.
3. A <-> B monotone cycle: peers read Current values, downstream Settled waits until the cycle is quiescent, and each evaluation is revision-caused.
4. Add an edge during ascent: standing values remain; only affected finality and content readers move.
5. Retraction/rebase: replacement reaches the correct fixed point without stale settled reads.

The tempting one-line change that sends readiness-only movement through enqueue_dependents(Current) must be tested first and rejected if it recalculates B on unchanged A; correctness alone is insufficient when the model promises minimal work.

## Telemetry acceptance

Consumes fz-kdt.34.

- readiness propagation and content wakes are distinguishable;
- a readiness-only change produces zero formula evaluations;
- every non-initial formula evaluation names a content revision that moved since its own prior conclusion;
- no full dependency scan occurs;
- repeated runs produce identical causal work traces.

## Documentation

Clarify Current content, local publisher cleanliness, and transitive finality as separate concepts. Remove the quiescent-group epoch proposal if this contract is satisfied without it.
